      "claim": "L4/L5 permeability records for related triterpenoid acids show moderate-to-good absorptive permeability (asiatic acid Caco-2 ~2×10^-5 cm/s; MCA rat Peff 1.13×10^-5 cm/s; oleanolic acid Papp 5.52×10^-6 cm/s), supporting the absorption component of the triterpenoid acid core.",
      "card_ids": ["C50","C53","C59","C65","C69"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance/metabolic-stability records are reference-molecule mechanistic data (BVM UGT glucuronidation, KZR-616 HLM Cl_int, artelinic acid CYP3A4, faldaprevir CLh, vicriviroc CYP3A4, pyridyl derivative 24 high Cl_int) without query-specific F endpoints; they do not provide affirmative evidence for F < 20% in the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Physicochemical liabilities (MW 730, logP 8.62, TPSA 125, zwitterionic character) are an uncertain prior, not endpoint proof, and do not override the transferable human L1 F records.",
      "card_ids": ["C18","C02","C05","C11","C12"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83"]
