    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux, intestinal metabolism, permeability, or solubility measurement is available; L4/L5 records are for reference molecules.",
    "The query's zwitterionic character, high TPSA, high MW, and high logP may reduce absorption relative to triterpenoid-acid references, but this is not experimentally quantified."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: all transferable human L1 records report F above 20%, including structurally relevant steroid acid UDCA (78–87%) and large lipophilic azole posaconazole (42–87%). L4/L5 add indirect absorption evidence for related triterpenoid acids, while L5 efflux and L6 hepatic-clearance records are reference-molecule mechanistic data without query-specific F endpoints. L2 low-F values are species- or formulation-specific, and physicochemical liabilities are an uncertain prior, not affirmative evidence for F < 20%."
}

